cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research, its data or its benchmark, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "RatLab — A Boar Research: an offline phone research assistant measured against 'half as good as internet + frontier AI' (research record and benchmark)"
abstract: >-
  Research record (v0.4-preprint, as of 2026-10-25; research lines closed by the author on
  2026-10-23) of BOAR, an offline Android research assistant built for poidh bounty #31
  ("more than 50 % as good as internet plus a frontier AI", at most 12 GB RAM, English).
  It covers two benchmarks (frozen frontier-plus-web references, a pairwise LLM judge in both
  presentation orders, pre-registered pass/fail rules; a second 75-item ruler written half by
  each judge family), about 390 recorded experiments, the decision log and the standing.
  As of 2026-10-25, under the Claude judge, the 0.50 bar was not reached on the earlier held-out sets
  and no unexposed held-out number exists: the frozen 4B build scores floor-adjusted 0.261
  (0.224-0.300), raw 0.413 (0.384-0.445), 0 wins of 51 on the bounty-style set (V-para, held-out
  at run time, 2 seeds, Claude Opus judge); a 35B deep tier with a 512-token thinking budget
  reaches floor-adjusted 0.436 (0.401-0.472) on development data, desktop only, and was not
  delivered. The author's thesis: small models need external knowledge, so the project built a
  harness around a small model's real capabilities, tuned for the app user's experience. Its
  evidence and limits come from closing tests on pack-written questions (Claude Haiku outcome
  labels, one seed): the 1.7B main engine is right on 65 % of items when search delivers the
  item's own article, which happens on 54 %, with no gain on real development items. The second
  ruler run on the desktop twin of the submitted app's pre-rename engine (b4ef94f3, one seed)
  won 0 of 71 under both judge families with a lower-family U-total of 0.164, below the bar
  (history); the headline is the same ruler measured on the phone with the submitted app,
  LabRat (formerly BoarLite), which is running (DEVICE-FINAL). See data/status.json.
